 "This prism is not magic, it does not bend light because of magic, it bends light because of the shape of the glass. The angle at which the glass is cut will bend the light at a particular angle."

This note is an example of:
A) A scientific explanation of the properties of prisms
B) A magical explanation of the properties of prisms
C) A philosophical discussion of the nature of light
D) A math problem to be solved

Correct answer: A) A scientific explanation of the properties of prisms

The note explains the scientific fact that the shape of the prism (specifically the angle at which it is cut) causes it to bend light. It does not suggest that the bending of light is due to magic, but rather provides a scientific explanation of the phenomenon. Option B) A magical explanation of the properties of prisms, which is the opposite of what the note actually says, and is not a correct answer. The other options are not correct because they are not accurate representations of what the note says. Therefore, option A) A scientific explanation of the properties of prisms is the correct answer. 2. What can we conclude about the student who wrote this note?

